# The php-paths example: PATHS to the bulk rebate in the helper Money::lineTotal, three of its
# four paths marked and taken as breakpoint sets (the test's left out): lavender, cyan and
# pink, the colours a new project's first sets get. The first request (invoice.print 1002)
# with lavender active, the second (order.show 1001) with cyan, then COMPARE of the two and
# TIMELINE in HISTORY. php-paths-flow.tsc follows.
@wait stop
/find Money.php:16
@key enter
/paths
@wait paths
@key space j space j space
@key enter
/view overview
# invoice.print 1002 stops 14 times, the breakpoints only in cyan and pink record.
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
@dump sets.ans
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
# order.show 1001 stops on its first line; cyan stops from here, 14 times.
/continue
@wait stop
/set active cyan
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@wait stop
/continue
@sleep 1000
/compare lavender cyan
@key j j j j j j j j
@dump compare.ans
/view history
@key tab j j j h
@dump timeline.ans
